        "text": "libraries with applications into a single file for cloud deployment, such as\nthe Java web archive file ( .war file). Another approach is to bundle all the\ndependencies containing application code and the target execution platform\ninto a container and deploy the container directly on a container hosting platform.\nWe will explore container-based deployment options in Chapter 11 , Using Python\nfor Microservices Development .\nThere are at least three options for deploying a Python web service application on GCP\nApp Engine, which are as follows:\n\u2022I Using the Google Cloud SDK via the CLI interface\n\u2022I Using the GCP web console (portal) along with Cloud Shell (CLI interface)\n\u2022I Using a third-party IDE such as PyCharm\nWe will discuss the first option in detail and provide a summary of our experience with\nthe other two options.\nImportant note\nTo deploy a Python application in AWS and Azure, the procedural steps are the\nsame in principle, but the details are different, depending on the SDK and API\nsupport available from each cloud provider.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Using Google Cloud SDK\n\u2022 Using the GCP web console\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
